      "math_academy_id": "e-7424",
      "problem": "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2} & =28 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2).$",
